6 44 here on a wednesday morning it's  time for our morning cup of joe's  segment with metro sheriff joe lombardo  we'll point out though this interview  was taped before this morning's officer  involved shooting  so we only have a few weeks left in the  school year ccsd says it wants to have  all of its students  back in class 100 percent in the next  school year in august  what discussions has metro started  having already with ccsd police  about the fall and about the look at  schools when the new year starts  yeah that's a constant conversation and  and i i got my fingers crossed hopefully  we do get all the  the students back into school at 100  percent and i think that's very  important for  their well-being their mindset and also  for the  families to be able to lack of a better  word babysit them  or have them to get the opportunity to  go back to work themselves and deal with  their life and  everything that goes along with it so  the most volatile or the most concerning  for us is to start a school when the  students are going to school and when  the students leave school  that seems to be when there's anxiety  emotion and trouble  associated with the students for us to  be concerned with so  you know and clark county school  district police are aware of that  and we work in conjunction with them we  have that omni presence  you know around the schools during those  time periods and we  are well involved when they do  extracurricular activities such as  football games and everything else that  goes along with it  that's not something you can ignore  because it's it's you know  used and emotionally and devil's  workshop with their hands if they're not  doing anything  to release their tensions and everything  else goes along with it  it's a it's a very important  consideration for us especially for the  school district police  and i don't want people in the community  to lose sight of that you know there's  there's conversations about getting  ready for the police and  in the school environment and i think  that would be a very uh  bad mistake i think it's a very  necessary entity  within that environment for for  everybody to feel safe and be successful  one thing that we hear a lot of  certainly when we're working on the  morning show  overnight we hear the scanners and these  reports of illegal shootings around the  valley  we've talked before about the shot  spotter technology what should folks in  the valley do  if they think they're hearing gunshots  in their neighborhood so they can stay  safe call us i mean that's a simple  answer i mean  a lot of things that we investigate or  successfully investigate is based on  pattern  if it's a one-off event it's very hard  for us to investigate and determine who  the perpetrator is but  and when we have numerous phone calls  and uh numerous people giving us  little bits of information that we can  compile together  uh it makes it a lot easier for us to  find the perpetrator and and it's  important for people to call us  it's just important for us to know that  because you mentioned the shot spotter  technology that's only in limited areas  in town  so it's not all-encompassing and it's  very important for us to have that  bigger  picture if you hear something if you see  something say something the same thing  goes if you hear something as well  sheriff lombardo thank you for joining  us again this morning we always  appreciate it you can submit some  questions for the sheriff yourself if  you'd like just head to 8newsnow.com  find out if your question is answered  every wednesday
 

